**Files changed:** `src/c_cp/c_cp.c` (created)

**Behavior implemented:**
- `SOURCE DEST` and `SOURCE... DIRECTORY` forms
- Multi-source requires last operand to be an existing directory (invocation-wide error otherwise)
- Two-operand form with directory destination: effective dest is `DIR/basename(SOURCE)`
- No options supported; any `-x` before `--` is an unknown option (status 1)
- `--` separates options from literal operands
- Bare `-` treated as filename
- Per-source copy via `copy_path`: follows source symlinks, rejects non-regular sources, rejects self-copy (same dev+ino), rejects dangling destination symlinks, rejects incompatible destination types, overwrites existing regular files retaining their permissions, creates new files with source permissions masked by umask
- Processes sources in operand order, continues after per-source failure, no rollback
- Exit status 0 on success, 1 on any failure
- 64 KiB read/write buffer, partial-write loop for robustness
- Arbitrary non-NUL pathname bytes preserved (all operations are byte-level)

**Interpretation chosen:** Since checkpoint 000 has zero implemented flags, any dash-prefixed token (other than bare `-`) before `--` is treated as an unknown option and triggers invocation-wide failure. No long options, no combined short options, no hidden options.
